Pages inspected: 7 (index, topic-01..04, unit-assessment, unit-teacher-notes)
at /semester-1/gict-300/unit-01/, three viewports each:

A. Desktop 1280x900 - all 7 pages HTTP 200; heading hierarchy has no skipped
   levels on every page; every <img> has non-empty alt; every visible figure
   loads (natural 249x150; the hidden .dark.svg twins are display:none by
   design and not defects); no vague link text. Advisory only: bare-URL link
   text in the per-topic Further reading citation lists.
B. Narrow 360x780 - document horizontal overflow 0px on all 7 pages; figures
   scale to client=328/scroll=328 (no spill, no scroller needed); no HTML
   content tables on these pages (all comparison tables are SVG figures).
C. A4 print 794px - clippedElems=0 on all 7 pages; every visible print figure
   fits (w=762, right=778); the Answers and marking guidance section and all
   four answer sub-headings render in print, not clipped.
D. SVG text geometry (all 8 figures, light + dark) - 6 figures clean in both
   variants; DEFECT in fig-U1-6 (light and dark): the axis label
   "more specialised" at x=686 runs to x=795.8, past the 780-unit viewBox
   right edge, so its tail is clipped when rendered.

Supplementary direct visual inspection (playwright-core element/viewport shots,
saved beside the render-inspect artifacts):
- fig-U1-6-element.png / fig-U1-6-label-corner.png: the rendered figure shows
  the label cut mid-word ("more specialis|") at the right edge, confirming the
